WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:19.650
Good morning Hank; it's Friday, January 12th.
If you're wondering why I'm drinking a beer

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.340
in the morning, it's because it's 12:15 in
the morning; I have to get up early tomorrow,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.460
so I'm doing the vlog tonight. If you're wondering
why I'm drinking light beer instead of regular

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:33.230
beer, it's because I'm doing Weight Watchers.
I don't like Weight Watchers. I'm tired of

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:37.120
eating popcorn. They don't give you enough
points! I need more points!

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.070
This video blog post is going to consist entirely
of ideas. Misprinted business card utilization

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:46.300
ideas: if you had a hole punch, a lot of patience,
and a lot of dental floss, you could make

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.440
Katherine a dress. You could eat them while
discussing the political situation in Kenya.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.280
Since you just got married, you can use them
to write very terse thank-you notes in very

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.579
small handwriting. You could wallpaper every
room in your dollhouse.

00:00:57.579 --> 00:00:59.969
Everybody thinks you have a dollhouse now!

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:04.739
Punishment ideas: I'm just going to pick punishment
ideas from things that are currently in our

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:05.739
living room.

00:01:05.739 --> 00:01:09.670
Several of our books would make excellent
punishments. This is The Continuum History

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:16.750
of Apocalypticism. It's eleven-hundred pages
long. It's pretty punishing.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:22.080
The person who fails to update has to send
out a Christmas card next year, and the Christmas

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:28.819
card has to include the picture of a baby,
someone else's baby. Maybe Emmitt Cloud's

00:01:28.819 --> 00:01:29.819
baby.

00:01:29.819 --> 00:01:33.550
The person who fails to update has to knit
a scarf. That would suck.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:37.060
The person who fails to update has to eat
one styrofoam peanut.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.300
And finally: Don't you think it would be a
good punishment if you had to do your Happy

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.220
Dance for three minutes and thirty seconds,
but you could only do it at five second clips

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:53.970
at a time, so you had to have a total of...
ah jeez, it's too late to call Daniel, hold

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:54.970
on.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:02:02.950
70? I think? 70 dances in 70 different locations?
That'd be a pretty good punishment. Or maybe

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:10.770
that should be a project? Maybe we could intersperse
our Happy Dances. You do 35, I do 35. That

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.590
has some appeal for me, any interest?

